ecast for May 2026 core PCE monthly inflation"},{"kind":"text","text":"The resolver is the BEA first print for Personal Income and Outlays, May 2026: PCE price index excluding food and energy, seasonally adjusted monthly percent change. This is a first-print forecast, so later BEA revisions should not alter the resolved value."},{"kind":"tool","tool":"official.lookup","call":"Checked BEA release schedule for the official May 2026 Personal Income and Outlays publication date.","result":"BEA schedule lists Personal Income and Outlays, May 2026 on June 25, 2026 at 8:30 AM; the same schedule page shows Personal Income and Outlays, June 2026 on July 30, 2026."},{"kind":"tool","tool":"official.lookup","call":"Checked BEA April 2026 Personal Income and Outlays release for latest official core PCE context.","result":"BEA reported April 2026 PCE price index +0.4 percent m/m, core PCE excluding food and energy +0.2 percent m/m, core PCE +3.3 percent y/y, and March core PCE +0.3 percent m/m in the release table."},{"kind":"tool","tool":"history.lookup","call":"Checked FRED mirror of BEA PCEPILFE index levels for recent monthly index context.","result":"FRED showed PCEPILFE Apr 2026 129.630, Mar 2026 129.321, Feb 2026 128.940, Jan 2026 128.432, Dec 2025 127.886; implied m/m changes are Apr 0.239 percent, Mar 0.295 percent, Feb 0.396 percent, Jan 0.427 percent."},{"kind":"tool","tool":"official.lookup","call":"Checked BLS May 2026 CPI release for source data relevant to core PCE nowcasting.","result":"BLS reported May 2026 CPI-U +0.5 percent m/m, core CPI +0.2 percent m/m, core CPI +2.9 percent y/y, shelter +0.3 percent m/m, medical care services +0.5 percent m/m, airline fares +2.7 percent m/m, and motor vehicle insurance -1.7 percent m/m."},{"kind":"tool","tool":"official.lookup","call":"Checked BLS May 2026 PPI release for producer-price components relevant to PCE mapping.","result":"BLS reported May 2026 final demand PPI +1.1 percent m/m, final demand goods +2.8 percent, final demand services +0.3 percent, final demand less foods energy and trade +0.8 percent, and portfolio management +4.8 percent."},{"kind":"text","text":"Base-rate/reference-class: recent core PCE monthly prints cluster between about 0.2 and 0.4 percent, with the FRED-implied latest four monthly changes at 0.239, 0.295, 0.396, and 0.427 percent. The April first print rounded to 0.2 percent despite firm headline PCE, so a May forecast should lean below the raw recent average but above the softer core CPI alone."},{"kind":"text","text":"Counter-consideration: May core CPI at 0.2 percent and declines in new vehicles, household furnishings, and motor vehicle insurance point to a low core PCE print. Against that, PPI services and portfolio-management prices were firm, and some PPI inputs feed more directly into PCE than CPI components do."},{"kind":"math","text":"Recent FRED-implied core PCE mean for Jan-Apr is (0.427 + 0.396 + 0.295 + 0.239) / 4 = 0.339 percent. I downweight that toward May core CPI of 0.2 because CPI was softer, while adding some PPI-services pressure: 0.55*0.24 latest core PCE momentum + 0.30*0.20 core CPI + 0.15*0.52 PPI-informed pressure = 0.270 percent. An 80 percent interval of 0.12 to 0.42 covers normal nowcast error and component-mapping uncertainty."},{"kind":"forecast","point":0.27,"ciLow":0.12,"ciHigh":0.42}]}
