.5 + 0.4*2.62 = 2.548, rounded to the agency precision as 2.5 percent. Set an 80 percent interval around recent monthly variation and one-print risk at 2.3 to 2.8 percent."},{"kind":"text","text":"Counter-consideration: the March-to-April decline from 2.7 to 2.5 could partly reverse in May, and the first print can move by 0.1 percentage point from sampling and seasonal adjustment noise even without a real labor-market turn."},{"kind":"forecast","point":2.5,"ciLow":2.3,"ciHigh":2.8}]}
