ment data.","result":"CMS states preliminary data are reported approximately 1 week after period close and updated data 1 month after close; the methodology page section spans lines 296-301 and distinguishes 2 data vintages."},{"kind":"tool","tool":"official.lookup","call":"Fetched the recent preliminary-vintage reference class from the official CMS data page for reporting periods 202511 through 202602.","result":"Official-source recent preliminary totals used were 78,620,000 for November 2025, 78,468,000 for December 2025, 78,312,000 for January 2026, and 78,184,000 for February 2026."},{"kind":"text","text":"Base rate: the comparable preliminary series was falling by about 128,000 to 156,000 per month across the latest three month-to-month moves, far below the steep unwinding losses of 2023-2024."},{"kind":"tool","tool":"official.lookup","call":"Checked the official monthly page and data links for release timing and target availability.","result":"As of the run, March 2026 was not yet listed; the official page's latest visible month was February 2026 and the latest visible update date was 2026-05-29, supporting the next fixed-vintage resolution on 2026-06-30."},{"kind":"text","text":"Level and momentum: starting from 78,184,000 in February, I carry forward a smaller decline than the recent average because unwinding-related attrition has largely normalized by early 2026."},{"kind":"text","text":"Policy and one-off mechanisms: upside would come from late state processing stabilization, continuous-eligibility effects, or stronger CHIP retention; downside would come from renewal backlogs, eligibility redeterminations, and state reporting corrections hitting the preliminary count."},{"kind":"math","text":"Recent monthly declines were roughly -152,000, -156,000, and -128,000, with an average near -145,000. I use a milder March decline of -124,000 from 78,184,000, giving 78,060,000. The 80% interval uses about +/-825,000, wider than recent momentum to cover state reporting dispersion and first-print noise: 78,060,000 - 810,000 = 77,250,000 and 78,060,000 + 840,000 = 78,900,000."},{"kind":"text","text":"Counter-consideration: if preliminary March captures more retroactive or late-processed enrollment than usual, the print could sit above February despite the broader downward trend; conversely, a cluster of state methodology changes could push the count below the interval."},{"kind":"text","text":"Outside-the-interval scenarios: below 77,250,000 would likely require unusually broad renewal-related terminations or a reporting break; above 78,900,000 would likely require a material state resubmission effect or a broad March enrollment rebound."},{"kind":"forecast","point":78060000,"ciLow":77250000,"ciHigh":78900000}]}
